# Required. Signs host tokens, and must be identical in the signaling service
# (ADR-0011). There is deliberately no development default: one would work
# locally, survive review, and reach production as a publicly known signing key.
#
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
SESSION_SECRET=

# Optional
# API_PORT=8788
# API_HOST=127.0.0.1
# APP_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# ICE configuration handed to clients (ADR-0004).
# STUN_URLS=stun:stun.l.google.com:19302

# The long-term Cloudflare key this service mints short-lived TURN credentials
# from, per request — never handed to a client itself. Optional: without it,
# /api/v1/ice-servers serves STUN-only, which still works between two
# friendly networks. `pnpm turn` sets both from `.env.turn` at the repo root —
# see dev-setup.md for the one-time dashboard setup.
# CLOUDFLARE_TURN_KEY_ID=
# CLOUDFLARE_TURN_API_TOKEN=
# TURN_CREDENTIAL_TTL_SECONDS=14400

# Where durable records go. Optional in development: without it the service
# runs with a no-op recorder and says so once at startup, so a fresh clone
# works with no Postgres installed.
#
#   docker compose -f infrastructure/docker-compose.dev.yml up -d
#   pnpm --filter @crossscreen/db migrate
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://crossscreen:crossscreen@localhost:5432/crossscreen

# Where errors go. Optional: without it, errors are still logged, just not
# reported anywhere durable — a fresh clone needs no Sentry account to run.
# Every event passes through @crossscreen/observability's scrubbing first: no
# tokens, no join codes, no IP addresses (phase-2-reliability.md §2.6).
# SENTRY_DSN=
